        {
          "kicker": "Opposition selection",
          "heading": "Fiji face debutant fly-half Domingo Miotti as Quesada tips tight Udine test",
          "body": "Italy head coach Gonzalo Quesada has handed a first cap to Domingo Miotti, the Montpellier fly-half eligible through his Italian grandfather, for today's Nations Championship test in Udine. A run of wing injuries pushed Ange Capuozzo out to the wing, with Tommaso Allan at full-back. Quesada called Fiji a quality side and expects a tight game. For head coach Jake White's Fiji, bottom of their pool without a point, defeat or a win without a bonus sets up an Italy rematch in the sixth-place final at Twickenham."
        },
