      "edition": "Saturday 21 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Captain's view",
          "heading": "Maro Itoje links clearer England purpose to four-win run before All Blacks",
          "body": "\"It feels a lot more cohesive,\" England captain Maro Itoje told BBC Rugby Union Weekly, saying the squad's understanding of its game plan has grown campaign by campaign. Four straight wins over Fiji, Argentina, Australia and Japan followed five successive Test defeats. Discipline tells the story: 14 yellow cards and a red in England's first eight Tests of 2026, then none in two November Tests. Head coach Steve Borthwick credits that turnaround to his senior players. New Zealand arrive on Saturday after their first defeat by Wales in 73 years."
        },
