    "387": {
      "date": "2026-11-21",
      "edition": "Saturday 21 November",
      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Comeback",
          "heading": "Anthony Jelonch back at No. 8 for France after shoulder surgery",
          "body": "Former France captain Anthony Jelonch starts at No. 8 against Argentina at the Stade de France, Planet Rugby reports. It is his first Test since he was injured against England in the Six Nations. He told Rugbyrama that a hamstring problem came first, followed by a shoulder operation that was delayed because a nerve had been affected. He spent the summer rehabilitating at the CERS in Capbreton, then made his club return against Exeter on 18 October. Esteban Capilla makes his first Test start at six in a reshuffled back row, with Charles Ollivon at seven."
        },
