      "sections": [
        {
          "kicker": "Debut call",
          "heading": "Quesada hands Domingo Miotti debut and Ortombina lineout role against Fiji",
          "body": "Italy head coach Gonzalo Quesada has made only two changes from the side beaten by Argentina for Saturday's Round 6 test against Fiji in Udine. Montpellier fly-half Domingo Miotti starts on debut in place of Paolo Garbisi. Alessandro Ortombina replaces Federico Ruzza, who drops to the bench. Quesada said Ortombina was picked to lead the lineout and bring physicality. Injuries to wings including Lynagh, Faissal, Pani and Trulla keep Ange Capuozzo on the wing, with Tommy Allan at full-back."
