          "kicker": "Age-grade win",
          "heading": "Scotland U20 beat Ireland U20 31-29 after trailing early in Cork",
          "body": "Fergus Pringle's Scotland U20 side recovered from a nervy start on Friday night at Virgin Media Park. Ireland U20 led 7-0 through full-back Fionn Rowsome, and the sides were level 19-19 at half-time before the visitors closed out the win. Rory Caldwell, James Dalrymple, Christian Lindsay and Rory McHaffie all scored tries, backed by Harry Clark's kicking. The Irish Times judged Scotland worthy winners, noting the side had six players back from the group that finished fifth at last summer's World Junior Championship."
        },
